11. Sub-section (3) of Section 3 of the Act of 1980 provides that if the Commissioner or the District Magistrate is satisfied that the conditions specified in clauses (a), (b) and (c) of sub-section (1) exist,
he may, by order in writing, amongst others, direct him to remove himself outside the district or part thereof, as the case may be, by such route, if any, and within such time as may be specified in the order and to desist from entering the district or the specified part thereof until the expiry of such period, not exceeding six months, as may be specified in the order.
